# Publishes this reactor's package-level guardrails for downstream consumers.
#
# Presence of this file is the opt-in. Each module writes one manifest per annotated package into
# its own class output. Under Gradle that is build/classes/java/main/vibetags/manifests/<pkg>.json,
# which the jar task packages with no further configuration; the Maven fixture's path is
# target/classes/. The two differ, which is why the Gradle side asserts on it rather than assuming
# the Maven fixture covers the publish step.
#
# The first non-blank, non-comment line is the artifact coordinate stamped into every manifest as
# "origin". Consumers render it next to each inherited rule so a reader can see which dependency is
# talking. Gradle projects can pass it as -Avibetags.manifest.origin instead, built from the
# project's own group/name/version; it is spelled out here so the example needs no build config to
# read.
#
# The version is deliberately two-segment and NOT the VibeTags release version. The origin string
# is rendered into every generated file of every consuming module, so a coordinate tracking the
# release would put the release version into committed demo files and oblige
# tools/set-version.sh to rewrite generated output, which ReleaseScriptCoverageTest refuses.
se.deversity.vibetags.example:gradle-multimodule-core:1.0
